engine marzano(0.1)
language ruby

// @dialect ruby
// Ruby sources (`.rb`) are parsed by the pinned upstream `tree-sitter-ruby`
// grammar (ABI 14) that the frozen Grit closure already carries. Grit returns
// syntax matches plus logged source values; Attune assigns repository
// identities, resolves and admits edges, and derives inverse relations one
// layer above this frontend.

// @syntax structural
//
// Explicit namespace and member declarations.
//
// All four forms define a symbol:
//
//   module Shop
//     module Pricing
//       def self.total_cents(items)
//         items.sum { |item| item }
//       end
//     end
//   end
//
//   class Receipt
//     def render(customer:, items:)
//       Pricing.total_cents(items)
//     end
//   end
//
// The match is the whole declaration and the logged value is its source name:
//
//   Shop
//   Pricing
//   total_cents
//   Receipt
//   render
//
// One log shape covers every form, so the canonical fact stays uniform. The
// declaration keyword is still recoverable, because the exact text between the
// declaration's start and its logged name is the keyword that wrote it:
//
//   module Shop                     -> "module "
//   class Receipt                   -> "class "
//   def self.total_cents(items)     -> "def self."
//   def render(customer:, items:)   -> "def "
//
// Attune's Flix resolver reads exactly that text: `module`/`class` opens a
// lexical namespace, `def self.` declares a class-level (singleton) method, and
// `def ` declares an instance method. Keyword parameters and block-bearing
// bodies change nothing about the declared name.
//
// Dynamically created or anonymous definitions have no stable repository name
// and are deliberately excluded:
//
//   define_method(:total_cents) { |items| items.sum }
//
//   Class.new { def render; end }
//
// Attune's Flix admission later assigns file and symbol identities, decides
// which namespace encloses each declaration, and derives the inverse relations.
//
// @example A nested module and its singleton method are two declarations.
// module Shop
//   module Pricing
//     def self.total_cents(items)
//       items.sum
//     end
//   end
// end
// @end

or {
  module(name = $name),
  class(name = $name),
  method(name = $name),
  singleton_method(name = $name)
} as $declaration where {
  log(message="definition", variable=$name)
}
